### TiendaBox - Pruebas del recurso Cart
### Todas las rutas requieren login como cliente.
### Ejecutar en orden: crea su propio producto de prueba (owner) y su propio
### cliente de prueba, y reutiliza tokens/ids automaticamente.

@host = http://localhost:3000
@clienteEmail = cart.test@example.com
@clientePassword = prueba123

### 1. Login owner -> 200 OK
# @name loginOwner
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@tiendabox.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}

### 2. Crear categoria de prueba (owner) -> 201 Created
# @name createCategory
POST {{host}}/api/category
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Cart Test Category {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 3. Crear marca de prueba (owner) -> 201 Created
# @name createBrand
POST {{host}}/api/brand
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Cart Test Brand {{$timestamp}}"
}

### 4. Crear producto de prueba con stock (owner) -> 201 Created
# @name createProduct
POST {{host}}/api/product
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "name": "Producto para carrito",
  "type": "stock",
  "price": 100,
  "stock": 5,
  "category_id": "{{createCategory.response.body.$.id}}",
  "brand_id": "{{createBrand.response.body.$.id}}"
}

### 5. Registrar cliente de prueba -> 201 Created
# Si ya existe de una corrida anterior, devuelve 409 (no afecta el caso 6).
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cart Test Cliente",
  "email": "{{clienteEmail}}",
  "password": "{{clientePassword}}"
}

### 6. Login cliente de prueba -> 200 OK
# @name loginCliente
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{clienteEmail}}",
  "password": "{{clientePassword}}"
}

### 7. Agregar item al carrito -> 200 OK
POST {{host}}/api/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}",
  "quantity": 2
}

### 8. Ver carrito -> 200 OK
GET {{host}}/api/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### 9. Agregar el mismo item de nuevo, suma cantidades -> 200 OK
POST {{host}}/api/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}",
  "quantity": 1
}

### 10. Agregar producto inexistente -> 400 Bad Request ("Producto no disponible")
POST {{host}}/api/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "product_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "quantity": 1
}

### 11. Agregar con cantidad invalida -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}",
  "quantity": 0
}

### 12. Agregar mas cantidad de la disponible en stock -> 400 Bad Request
POST {{host}}/api/cart/items
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

{
  "product_id": "{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}",
  "quantity": 999
}

### 13. Quitar item del carrito -> 200 OK
DELETE {{host}}/api/cart/items/{{createProduct.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### 14. Vaciar carrito -> 204 No Content
DELETE {{host}}/api/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{loginCliente.response.body.$.token}}

### 15. Acceder sin token -> 401 No autenticado
GET {{host}}/api/cart

### 16. Acceder como owner, no cliente -> 403 No autorizado
GET {{host}}/api/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOwner.response.body.$.token}}
